  "findings": [
    "Two new access maps and dotted overviews: Banks–Beehive Bend and Danskin–Confluence.",
    "Four official facility-area markers added with distinct site identities and coordinate provenance.",
    "Five South Fork branches reviewed; main-stem takeout anchor avoids a nearer Middle Fork flowline while retaining the public facility pin.",
    "Agency guide distances of 7.3 and 13 miles retained; source overview lengths differ by less than two percent.",
    "Riggins–Lucile difficulty corrected from Class II–III to Class II–IV based on BLM map 11. Its access map remains held."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Local review only; no publishing.",
    "Approximate facility areas, not surveyed shore landings or bank-side instructions.",
    "No gauge, calibration, planning mileage, live timing or GPS ETA changes.",
    "Dotted lines are display-only, not rapid-running or navigation routes.",
    "Seasonal access and fees need a current check before a trip."
  ],
  "nextResearch": [
    "Riggins City Ramp is documented on BLM guide map 10, but a defensible coordinate still needs to be recorded; the 2026 georeferenced Vinegar–Pine Bar PDF is saved for this.",
    "Lucile agency web-page coordinate differs from GIS by over a kilometre; GIS and map 13 identify the intended recreation site. Keep it separate from Old Lucile.",
    "IDFG all-sites inventory and USFS/BLM records saved for additional Idaho access research. Clearwater town labels need specific facility identities, not nearest unrelated ramps."
  ]
